<p>
  Paid costs $<%= StripeBilling::PRICE_PER_SEAT_USD %> per user
  per month, with a <%= StripeBilling::TRIAL_PERIOD_DAYS %>-day free trial and
  no automatic per-document overage charges. Business costs $<%= StripeBilling::BUSINESS_BASE_USD %>
  per month with one seat included; extra seats cost $<%= StripeBilling::PRICE_PER_SEAT_USD %>
  per month. Everything to do with money lives on
  <strong>Settings &rarr; Billing</strong>.
</p>

<h2>Starting the trial</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Open <strong>Settings &rarr; Billing</strong> and choose <strong>Start <%= StripeBilling::TRIAL_PERIOD_DAYS %>-day free trial</strong>.</li>
  <li>Enter your card on Stripe's own secure page. Card details never touch EsignCenter.</li>
  <li>You come straight back and the paid features are on. The billing page shows the day the trial ends and what it will cost after that.</li>
</ol>

<p>
  We ask for a card at the start because the trial turns into a subscription
  when it ends. Cancel before that day and you are not charged at all. There is
  one trial per account, ever.
</p>

<h2>Managing your subscription</h2>

<p>
  <strong>Manage billing</strong> opens the Stripe Customer Portal, where you
  can update the card, download every invoice and receipt, correct your invoice
  details, and cancel. Seats are not editable there because your seat count is
  simply the number of people in your account &mdash; see
  <%= link_to 'Teams and seats', help_article_path('teams-and-seats') %>.
</p>

<h2>Plans and API capacity</h2>

<p>
  Paid includes <%= Quotas::Limits::PAID_API_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> API completions a month;
  Business includes <%= Quotas::Limits::BUSINESS_API_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %>, per billing account.
  API, embedded signing and MCP count once at the first signature per document lineage.
  Allowances reset on the first day of each UTC calendar month. Documents already sent always finish.
  Open API documents reserve capacity until signed, declined, expired or archived. At the allowance, new API documents pause; corrections of signed documents and in-app Resubmit remain available.
</p>
<p>
  In Billing settings, upgrading to Business charges the prorated difference now. Moving to Paid
  takes effect at renewal with no credit, and Business capacity stays until then. Recurring API packs cost
  $<%= StripeBilling::API_PACK_USD %> per month for <%= Quotas::Limits::API_PACK_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %>
  extra completions. Each added pack costs the full monthly price now, with no proration, and is
  available after payment. This applies during a trial too: packs are paid for when added, the trial
  continues, and packs renew monthly once it ends.
  Removing packs takes effect at renewal. If your API capacity is set by an agreement, contact us
  to change it. Purchase controls appear when the plan or packs are available.
</p>

<h2>Cancelling and refunds</h2>

<p>
  You can cancel at any time. Your paid access continues to the end of the
  period you have already paid for, and then the account moves to the free
  plan. Nothing is deleted: every document, template and export stays readable,
  downloadable and exportable. Cancelling during the trial costs nothing. After
  the trial there are no prorated refunds for a period you have started &mdash;
  the exact wording is in the <%= link_to 'Terms', terms_path %>.
</p>

<aside class="help-callout">
  <p>
    <strong>Good to know:</strong> if our systems ever charge you twice for the
    same subscription, we refund the duplicate &mdash; automatically where we
    can and by hand where we cannot. That is not a goodwill gesture we may
    decline; it is written into the Terms as what we do.
  </p>
</aside>

<h2>If a payment fails</h2>

<p>
  A failed renewal does not take the product away on day one. Stripe keeps
  retrying the card and you get
  <%= BillingLifecycle::PAST_DUE_GRACE_DAYS %> days of grace, during which
  everything works exactly as before, paid features included. We email your
  administrators <%= BillingLifecycle::DUNNING_DAYS.size %> times in that
  window, each message naming the date the account would be suspended and
  linking straight to the billing page.
</p>

<p>
  On day <%= BillingLifecycle::PAST_DUE_GRACE_DAYS %> the account becomes
  read-only, and nothing more than that: everybody can still sign in, read,
  download and export; a signer already holding one of your documents can still
  finish it; nothing new can be created. Paying lifts it automatically, within
  seconds &mdash; no support ticket, no manual step.
</p>

<h2>Going back to free</h2>

<p>
  When a paid plan ends, your free-plan month starts at that moment: you begin
  at 0 of <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> completions and 0
  of <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SENDS_PER_MONTH %> sends, whatever you did
  earlier in the calendar month. The free month still ends with the calendar
  month. See <%= link_to 'Free plan limits', help_article_path('free-plan-limits') %>
  and the <%= link_to 'pricing page', pricing_path %>.
</p>
